      "worked": "The domain is $x\\ne-2$. The absolute-value inequality gives two cases.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^2-x+2}{x+2}&\\le-4\\\\\\frac{x^2+3x+10}{x+2}&\\le0\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $x^2+3x+10=\\left(x+\\frac32\\right)^2+\\frac{31}{4}>0$, this case requires $x<-2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^2-x+2}{x+2}&\\ge4\\\\\\frac{x^2-5x-6}{x+2}&\\ge0\\\\\\frac{(x-6)(x+1)}{x+2}&\\ge0\\end{align*}$$\n\nChecking signs across $-2$, $-1$ and $6$ gives $-2<x\\le-1$ or $x\\ge6$.\n\nTherefore, $x<-2$ or $-2<x\\le-1$ or $x\\ge6$.",
